Package: moira
Version: 0.3.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Thibault Paul <xpaul.thibault@gmail.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-secret-1
Description: Claude and Codex quota monitor
 Moira is a compact Ubuntu GTK4/Libadwaita utility showing Claude and Codex
 quota usage, local reset times, countdowns, refresh state and weekly
 exhaustion semantics. Data comes only from structured provider surfaces:
 the chained Claude Code status-line command and the documented Codex
 app-server read-only rate-limit method. Missing or invalid data is shown
 as Unavailable, Parse error or Stale — never invented.
 .
 It adds a History tab with selectable 24h/7d/30d/90d ranges and per-service
 filters, quota series with reset transitions, availability states, exact
 daily token statistics computed only from official Codex account usage
 (Claude remains percentage-only), sanitized diagnostics with copy actions,
 and deterministic CSV/JSON export.
 .
 Per-provider collection toggles, typed alert rules, and native desktop and
 NTFY notification channels provide deduplicated exhaustion, recovery,
 reset and error events. Manual update checks use strict SemVer parsing.
 .
 Privacy-minimal agent activity is shown for Claude Code, Hermes and
 Moira-owned Codex app-server sessions through owned hooks and the
 documented Codex app-server protocol: only hashed session and turn
 identities, sanitized model labels and UTC timestamps are stored, and the
 activity is watched live with no polling or terminal scraping. Independent
 Codex CLI sessions are never observed.
 .
 Configuration is versioned JSON (config v3), History is stored in a
 versioned SQLite database (schema v4), and all user files are preserved
 across upgrades. The interface is localized in French with English
 fallback.
